jt-pve-storage-synology (0.5.5~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * 0.5.3~beta1 and 0.5.4~beta1 could not be used: pvesm add failed with
    "missing value for required option 'syno-password'" because PVE strips
    sensitive properties before validating required ones. Declared optional and
    enforced by the plugin.
  * CHAP was applied only when the target was created, so adding it to an
    existing storage gave no error and no access control. ensure now reconciles
    it, and the update hook pushes the secret to every target.
  * Refuse a CHAP username with no secret before writing anything.
  * Compute the effective config in the update hook: PVE applies deletions after
    the hook, so --delete of both CHAP options refused itself.

